{
  "_comment": [
    "HAND-AUTHORED SPECIFICATION FIXTURE — MODULES.json M1, DESIGN.md §8.",
    "",
    "This is not a sample of the real corpus and it is not generated from one. It is a",
    "minimum corpus that exercises every branch of the loader and the planner, so that M2,",
    "M3 and M4 can be built and tested before Phase B saturation is anywhere near the",
    "engine. 40 records.",
    "",
    "What it deliberately covers:",
    "  - all four pov stances, including `second`, of which the REAL corpus's original 612",
    "    records had exactly zero. That is why the center lane needed authoring at all.",
    "    (20/44 basic, 45/74 light, 75/109 moderate, 110/149 deep, 150/200 extreme).",
    "  - `induction` and `emergence` as first-class themes, so the phase bookends have",
    "    something to play. Without these no session plans at all (§4.2).",
    "  - 2 multi-tagged records (`this_yes_arrives_before_the_question` and",
    "    `every_command_lands_where_focus_already_is`), so the cross-tag exclusion path is",
    "    live: exclusions check a mantra's FULL tag list, not the bucket it was collected",
    "    under. The real corpus was single-tag on all 612, leaving that path unexercised.",
    "  - invariant records at three tiers, so the drift-pivot's neutral preference (§4.6)",
    "    and unison's redraw refusal (§4.7) both have material to work on.",
    "  - four titration themes each holding >= 8 records, which is T1's ship floor, so a",
    "    theme block can serve a triplet without adjacency widening.",
    "",
    "`_comment` keys are ignored by the loader: it validates the five real record fields and",
    "reads nothing else off the file.",
    "",
    "The sidecar for this file is fixtures/persons.mini.json, and it satisfies",
    "persons[id][record.markers.pov] === record.text for all 40 records."
  ],
